# Changelog discipline

Whenever you change application behavior, UI, APIs, scripts, or user-facing docs in this repo, **update [`Changelog.md`](Changelog.md) in the same turn** — before considering the task done. Do not wait for the user to ask.

## No Unreleased — ship immediately

- Do **not** use a `## [Unreleased]` section.
- Every meaningful change batch is a **released** entry: `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD` at the top.
- Bump `app.__version__` to the same `X.Y.Z` in the same turn.
- SemVer: patch for fixes, minor for new features, major for breaking changes. Prefer **minor** for user-visible features, **patch** for fixes-only.

## Format (Keep a Changelog)

- Follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/) + [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).
- Newest version first.
- Groups under a version: `Added`, `Changed`, `Deprecated`, `Removed`, `Fixed`, `Security`.
- Omit empty groups.
- Write for humans: what changed and why it matters — not file lists or commit hashes.

## What must be logged

- User-visible behavior (GUI, dialogs, status text, install/run scripts)
- New or changed Git actions / safety confirmations
- Bug fixes the user would notice
- Security-related changes (vault, PAT handling)

## What may be skipped

- Typos in comments only
- Pure refactors with no behavior change
- Test-only changes that do not alter product behavior
- Formatting / lint-only edits

## Same-turn checklist

```text
□ Code change done
□ New ## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD section at top of Changelog.md
□ app.__version__ set to X.Y.Z
```

## Example entry

```markdown
## [1.3.0] - 2026-08-17

### Added

- Open project folder in Explorer from the dashboard card

### Fixed

- Pull uses the current branch instead of a stale stored default
```
